From cdc3d676627a20c7337770eb7e9483d85d89e63f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aleksei Bukhalov <buhaloff.aleks@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 16:28:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] feat: optional dequantize-on-promote for quantized disk
 entries

A quantized disk entry normally stays a QuantizedKVCache for the rest
of the conversation once promoted into RAM. --prompt-cache-disk-
dequantize-on-promote converts it back to a plain KVCache at
promotion time instead, via mx.dequantize -- an alternative to weigh
against the quality/speed tradeoff of staying quantized, not a
strict improvement over it.
---
 mlx_lm/prompt_cache_disk.py     | 38 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 mlx_lm/server.py                | 13 +++++++++++
 tests/test_prompt_cache_disk.py | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 88 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

